From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: tests can keep full screen to some displays

What: OMACVM_TEST_ONLY_DISPLAYS=ID,ID,... gives windows only to those Mac
displays, with real full screen (Spaces, menu bar, Dock) unlike
OMACVM_TEST_SKIP_DISPLAYS. Unset: no change.

Why: a full-screen test on the MacBook and its external monitor must not
put a window on another test's virtual display (it would cover that test's
VM window).

Upstream: not applicable (test hook of OmacVM's display windows).
Test: used by the display tests (notes: display-bugs track).

diff --git a/ui/cocoa.m b/ui/cocoa.m
index 0aca169..094a91d 100644
--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -3245,6 +3245,18 @@ static bool omacvm_test_mode(void)
 static bool omacvm_test_allows(CGDirectDisplayID id)
 {
     const char *v = getenv("OMACVM_TEST_SKIP_DISPLAYS");
+    const char *only = getenv("OMACVM_TEST_ONLY_DISPLAYS");
+
+    /* Real full screen, but only on these displays (others' test displays stay alone). */
+    if (only && *only) {
+        for (NSString *s in [[NSString stringWithUTF8String:only]
+                             componentsSeparatedByString:@","]) {
+            if ((CGDirectDisplayID)[s longLongValue] == id) {
+                return true;
+            }
+        }
+        return false;
+    }
     if (!v || !*v) {
         return true;
     }
